  {
   "rule": "An adjective (<em>naʿt</em>) comes <strong>after</strong> its noun and copies it: definite with definite, indefinite with indefinite, feminine with feminine, and the same case ending. If the noun has <span class='ar'>الْ</span> and the description doesn't, you have a sentence (“is”); if both have it, it's just a phrase."
  },
